Okay, building barback.
Building an app that will help with my Lead Bartending duties. 
Inventory - display well bottles forefront with par levels - alarm when par is low. 
Ai Integreation - add ingredients, this will build a cocktail, api call 
Cognito user pools - indentity center - seperate owner from employee
AWS Budget
AWS CloudTrail - monitor and seperate from architecture (further protection from deleting trail)

## Build 1: SAM foundation
SAM skeleton for CloudFormation
/health is route/path. standard health check
api address / path 

- template.yaml = IaC
- Transform = expands SAM shorthand into full CludFormation
- Globals = shared settings for every function - x-ray
- HttpApi = API
- HealthFunction = /health code
 - CodeUri = which folder, Handler app.handler = file app.py
- !Ref = get another resource's ID; !Sub = fill values into the string
- Outputs = print useful values (ApiUrl) after deploy
- Commands: sam validate --lint > sam build > sam deploy > --config-env dev
- samconfig.toml = saved deploy answers (stack barback-dev, us-west-2)
- Test: /health returned "ok"

## Build 2: Cognito sign-in
UserPool = email login, password (+12 char), optional MFA, email recovery, custom barId = which bar a user works at

- UserPoolClient - the door React uses
  - no secret (browsers can't hide one)
  - WriteAttributes [email] = users can't change their own barId
  - PreventUserExistenceErrors = hides whether an email is registered
- OwnerGroup / StaffGroup = role badges
- JWT authorizer on HttpApi = hides whether an email is registered
- /health = Auth NONE (public); /me = needs a token, returns this claims
- Test: /health ok, /me without token 401 unauthorized
- Test user: +owner email, CONFIRMED, group owner, barId bar-001